#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kronometer; is a stopwatch for &kde;. It can be used for basic tasks like "
"timer start/pause/resume, as well as lap times recording."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kronometer; is able to save a complete session (timer and lap times) and to "
"restore it later."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: index.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid "<keyword>KDE</keyword>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: index.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid "Kronometer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: index.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid "stopwatch"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:57
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kronometer; is a simple stopwatch application. It is meant to be simple and "
"pleasant to use, thanks to a use cases driven development."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kronometer; main features are the following:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kronometer; provides a timer that can be started, paused, resumed and reset."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kronometer; allows you to record lap times and export them to a file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kronometer; allows you to save a session and restore it later."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kronometer; allows you to copy timer numbers from display."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid "General Usage"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kronometer; main use case is of course the interaction with the timer. You "
"can start/pause/resume the timer by clicking on the proper actions in the "
"toolbar or in the &kronometer; menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Even simpler, you can use the keyboard instead of the mouse: you start the "
"timer with the keyboard's <keycap>Space</keycap> and you pause the timer "
"with <keycap>Space</keycap> too. You might recognize this behavior from many "
"media player applications."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By pressing the <keycap>Enter</keycap> key when the timer is running, you "
"freeze that particular time and you create a new <emphasis>lap</emphasis> "
"time. These times are always visible in the table on the left of the "
"application, where you can sort them by clicking the <emphasis>Lap time</"
"emphasis> column's header. You can also add a custom text annotation to each "
"lap, by double-clicking the cells within the <emphasis>Note</emphasis> "
"column."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid "Save and restore sessions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you pause a running stopwatch you create a session: a stopwatch time "
"and zero or more lap times. You can save a session on a file and you can "
"restore it later."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid "Save a session"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Pause a running stopwatch, then click on the <guibutton>Save As</guibutton> "
"button on the toolbar or in the <guimenu>File</guimenu> menu. Then choose a "
"name for the session's file to be stored on your computer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restore a session"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click the <guibutton>Open</guibutton> button on the toolbar or in the "
"<guimenu>File</guimenu> menu. Then choose an existing session's file to be "
"loaded."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid "Update a session"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the session is restored, you can resume the stopwatch and you can "
"record new lap times. If you want to save the updated session, you can "
"simply click the <guibutton>Save</guibutton> button in the toolbar or in the "
"<guimenu>File</guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid "Export lap times"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you record one or more lap times, the export features in the "
"<guimenu>File</guimenu> menu is made available, under the entry "
"<guimenuitem>Export laps as</guimenuitem>. Click on it and then choose a "
"name for the exported file. You can export in the Comma Separated Values "
"(CSV) format or in the &XML; one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid "Clipboard support"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kronometer; is able to copy the current stopwatch time to the system "
"clipboard. Use the <keycombo>&Ctrl;<keycap>C</keycap></keycombo> key "
"combination or the <guimenuitem>Copy</guimenuitem> entry in the "
"<guimenu>Edit</guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kronometer; is customizable in many aspects. You can open the settings "
"dialog clicking on the <guimenuitem>Configure &kronometer;</guimenuitem> "
"entry in the <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> menu. The settings dialog is "
"organized in the following categories."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid "General settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the general settings page you can choose the preferred time format for "
"the stopwatch display and for the lap times. You choose whether to show "
"hours, minutes, seconds or second fractions. &kronometer; supports time "
"granularity up to millisecond, although it requires high CPU usage due to "
"the high refresh rate of the UI."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid "Font settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the font settings page you can customize the font of the stopwatch "
"display. You can choose different font families, styles and sizes for each "
"timer component (hours, minutes, &etc;)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid "Color settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the color settings page you can customize the default color of the "
"stopwatch display. You can change the background color and the text color."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid "Interface settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the interface settings page you can choose whether to disable the laps "
"recording feature. This can be useful if you wish to optimize the window "
"content. You can also choose whether to show the time headers. The time "
"headers are the labels on the upper space of the stopwatch display. They "
"show the name of each timer component (hours, minutes, &etc;)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:170
#, no-c-format
msgid "Save settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the save settings you can choose the indentation size (that is the number "
"of blank spaces) of the XML files created by &kronometer;. The dialog allows "
"you to choose different sizes for the <emphasis>save files</emphasis> and "
"the <emphasis>export files</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also set the indent size (number of characters) of the &XML; save "
"files and exported files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kde; Built-in settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kronometer; makes use of the standard &kde; configuration tools. You find "
"them in the <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> menu, under the "
"<guimenuitem>Configure shortcuts</guimenuitem> and <guimenuitem>Configure "
"Toolbars</guimenuitem> entries. They allow you to change the shortcuts of "
"the &kronometer;'s actions, and to change the position of the toolbar and "
"its content."
msgstr ""

